Patch 6017: a title port may serve a read-only cellFs file through a virtual view (g_ps3_fs_vfile_ops, NULL by default).

New header include/ps3emu/fs_vfile.h: a provider with open, size, read and close. cellFsOpen offers each read-only open (no O_TRUNC)
to the provider after the host file is open; when it claims the path, the fd keeps its real host FILE* (the fd table, Write, Fsync and
the logs work as before) and Read, Lseek, Fstat and AioRead go through the provider: the guest's position is kept per fd (under the
fd's stream lock, held for a virtual fd even with FS_STREAM_LOCK=0), SEEK_END and Fstat use the virtual size, and a read is clamped to
the virtual size before the provider is asked, so a read that crosses the end returns the short count. AioRead reads the virtual bytes
and does not move the position. Close releases the view; a re-open is a new view. cellFsSdataOpen never serves a virtual file and logs
one line when the provider would have claimed its path. An fd keeps the ops it was opened with until it is closed. With the pointer
NULL: one atomic load per open and one per Read/Lseek/Fstat/Close/AioRead, nothing else changes (the existing test_fs_* pass unchanged).
Use in J-Stars: mods override entries inside the game's CPK archives without writing to them (the provider serves the original bytes,
a TOC with the overridden rows rewritten, and the mod data appended); J-Stars bounds its reads by the Fstat size, so the virtual size
must come from Fstat. Upstream candidate (general: "serve a file through a port-provided view").
Test: runtime/ppu/tests/test_fs_vfile.cpp (tools/test_ppu_fs_vfile.py; installer/tools/fs_vfile_test.sh also runs the other test_fs_*).

